<ul dir="auto">
<li><strong>Unpaid subscriptions</strong>: when Stripe stops retrying and marks a subscription unpaid instead of cancelling it, PulseMRR counts it as a failed payment, not a cancellation, from the period it didn't pay. It shows in <strong>To recover</strong> for 90 days, since its invoice can still be paid; paid later, it's the same customer, never counted as new.</li>
<li><strong>Card checks</strong>: an authorization made at a trial's start and released right away no longer shows as a sale followed by a refund.</li>
</ul>
      ]]></description>
